               <persName xml:id="n1" xml:lang="ar">ابن حجر الهيتمي, ابو العباس احمد بن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن حجر شهاب الدين الهيتمي السعدي</persName>
               <persName corresp="#n1" type="transliterated">Ibn Ḥaǧar al-Haytamī, Abū al-ʻAbbās Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʻAlī b. Ḥaǧar Šihāb al-Dīn al-Haytamī al-Saʻdī</persName>
               <floruit>10th /16th century (d. 973 / 1565)<note>Famous scholar and prolific writer of the Šāfiʿī school. He studied the usual branches of Islamic and Arabic learning, and also medicine. While still a child, he lost his father and then his grandfather, but his father’s teachers, Šams al-Dīn b. Abī al-Ḥamāʾil (d. 932/1526), a noted mystic, and Šams al-Dīn Muḥammad al-Šanāwī, a disciple of this last, looked after his maintenance and education.</note>
               </floruit>
               <birth evidence="internal" calendar="hijri" when-custom="0909-07">0909-07 </birth>
               <death calendar="hijri" when-custom="0973-07-23">0973-07-23 </death>
